## Breaking Changes in Microsoft.OpenApi v2 (shipped with .NET 10)

The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package depends on **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which adopted OpenAPI 3.1 / JSON Schema and removed several legacy types. Here's each issue and its fix:

### 1. `OpenApiString` and `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` removed
All `IOpenApiAny` types (`OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc.) are gone. Use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` instead.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After (.NET 10)
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `Schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema's type-union model. Nullability is now a flag on `Schema.Type`.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (.NET 10) — remove the Null flag from Type
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

You'll need:
```csharp
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;  // JsonSchemaType lives here
```

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a dictionary
It no longer inherits from `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>`. Use its `Schemes` property instead.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// After (.NET 10)
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new()
    {
        Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
        {
            [oAuthScheme] = scopes
        }
    }
};
```

### 4. `ReferenceType` → `ReferenceType` enum values renamed
The enum moved and some values were renamed to match the OpenAPI 3.1 spec terminology.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }

// After (.NET 10)
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
// ↑ This specific value is unchanged, but verify your usings —
//   it's still in Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References namespace.
```

---

### Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new()
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of changes:**
| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `new OpenApiString("…")` | `JsonValue.Create("…")` |
| `schema.Nullable = false` | `schema.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `new() { [scheme] = scopes }` | `new() { Schemes = { [scheme] = scopes } }` |
| `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `using System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
